---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const CONTACT = "oneabovealldotorg@gmail.com";
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Terms — oneaboveall"
  heading="Terms of Service"
  description="The rules of oneaboveall.org: how the daily auction for the center seat works, why you pay only if you win, and what you may put in the picture."
  lastUpdated="October 2, 2026"
>
  <p>
    These terms are the agreement between you and us when you use
    oneaboveall.org (the "site"). Please read them before you bid. By signing
    in or placing a bid you agree to them, and to our
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    The site is operated by <strong>Devvally</strong>, based in Spain ("we",
    "us"). You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Who can take part</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone can look at the site. To sign in and bid you must be
    <strong>at least 18 years old</strong> and able to enter into a binding
    contract, and you must use a payment card you are authorized to use. One
    person, one account. We may suspend or close accounts that break these
    terms, try to manipulate the auction, or use someone else's identity or
    card.
  </p>

  <h2>3. What the site is</h2>
  <p>
    oneaboveall.org is a single, continuously redrawn artwork: a crowd with
    one person in the center. The center seat is sold through a never-ending
    auction. Winning buys a <strong>paid placement of your likeness in the
    artwork</strong> — your photo is used to redraw the person in the center —
    and a public mention of your display name (and, if you add one, a social
    link) for as long as you hold the seat.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How the auction works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      There is one round per day. Each new bid must beat the current price by
      at least <strong>$1</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Bidding closes every day at <strong>4:00 PM US Eastern Time</strong>.
      Bids that reach us after the close don't count for that round.
    </li>
    <li>
      The highest valid bid at the close wins the round. If nobody bids, the
      current person stays in the center and a new round starts.
    </li>
    <li>
      The winner uploads a photo (if they haven't already) and the scene is
      redrawn with them in the center, usually around
      <strong>7:00 PM Eastern Time</strong> the same day. Timing may slip if
      we need to review the photo or if something goes wrong technically.
    </li>
    <li>
      The winner keeps the seat until someone outbids them in a later round.
      There is no guaranteed minimum time in the seat.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your display name is shown publicly while you lead a round, when you
      hold the seat, and on the leaderboard and history of past champions.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Payments — you pay only if you win</h2>
  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>When you bid, your card is only authorized (a temporary hold),
      not charged.</strong> You are charged only if you hold the top bid when
      bidding closes at 4:00 PM ET.
    </p>
  </div>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Payments are processed by Stripe. We never see or store your full card
      number.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>At the close</strong>, we capture (charge) the hold of the
      round's top bidder. That is the only charge.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>If you're outbid</strong>, we release your hold. The bidder
      immediately behind the leader may have their hold kept until the close
      as a fallback: if the winner's card fails, we charge the next-highest
      bid instead. All remaining holds are released once the round is
      settled.
    </li>
    <li>
      A released hold is never charged, but your bank decides how fast it
      disappears from your statement — usually instantly, sometimes a few
      business days.
    </li>
    <li>
      Prices are in US dollars. Your bank may add currency-conversion fees;
      those are outside our control.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Once you win and are charged, the payment is final.</strong> We
      refund a winning payment only (a) if we remove your content for breaking
      these terms <em>before</em> it is published in the artwork, or (b) where
      the law requires it. Being outbid later is how the auction works and is
      not a reason for a refund.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Your right of withdrawal (EU/UK consumers)</h2>
  <p>
    Consumers in the EU and UK normally have 14 days to withdraw from an
    online contract. Because the auction is a service performed on a fixed
    daily schedule, when you bid you
    <strong>ask us to start performing the service immediately</strong> and
    you <strong>acknowledge that you lose your right of withdrawal once the
    service has been fully performed</strong> — that is, once you win the
    seat at the close. Until then you are not charged anything at all.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Content rules — photos, names and links</h2>
  <p>You are responsible for the photo, display name, description and link you give us. They must not contain or point to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>nudity or sexual content;</li>
    <li>hate speech, harassment, or content that demeans people for who they are;</li>
    <li>violence, gore, or threats;</li>
    <li>impersonation of another person, brand or organization;</li>
    <li>other people's faces or likeness without their permission;</li>
    <li>anyone under 18;</li>
    <li>anything illegal, or that infringes someone else's rights (copyright, trademark, privacy);</li>
    <li>scams, phishing, malware, or misleading links.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    When you upload a photo you confirm that you have the right to use it and
    that everyone in it has agreed. You give us a worldwide, non-exclusive,
    royalty-free licence to use, adapt and redraw it into the artwork, and to
    show the resulting artwork (including in our own promotion of the site)
    for as long as it is displayed and in the archive of past scenes. You keep
    ownership of your photo.
  </p>
  <p>
    We review what is submitted and may, at our discretion, refuse,
    moderate, edit, remove, or redraw any content, display name or link —
    including after publication — if we believe it breaks these rules or the
    law. Reports: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Sponsored creators</h2>
  <p>
    We sometimes pay creators to promote the site. When a sponsored creator
    appears on the site (for example as the leader or champion), they are
    marked <strong>"Sponsored creator"</strong>. Sponsored creators bid under
    the same rules as everyone else.
  </p>

  <h2>9. This is not gambling</h2>
  <p>
    The site is not a lottery, game of chance or prize draw. What you pay for
    is a placement in an artwork, sold to the highest bidder. There is no
    prize, nothing is won by chance, and the seat has no cash value and
    cannot be exchanged for money.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Chargebacks</h2>
  <p>
    If something is wrong with a charge, please email us first — we'll sort
    it out. If you dispute a valid winning charge with your bank instead, we
    may remove your content from the artwork and suspend your account while
    the dispute is open.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Availability and liability</h2>
  <p>
    We provide the site "as is". We do our best to keep it running and the
    auction on schedule, but we can't promise it will always be available or
    error-free. If a technical problem affects a round, we may extend, rerun
    or cancel that round; if we cancel it, any holds are released and nobody
    is charged.
  </p>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or
    consequential losses, and our total liability to you is limited to the
    amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim. Nothing in these
    terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law, or your statutory
    rights as a consumer.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. The date at the top shows the latest version.
    Changes apply from that date to new bids; a round you are already bidding
    in keeps the terms that applied when you bid.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of Spain. If you are a consumer, you
    also keep the protection of the mandatory laws of the country you live in
    and may bring a claim in your local courts.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, complaints or content reports:
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
